## 0. Data principle (UPDATED — product decision)

> **عربي:** قسم — Primary (the base)

### Primary (the base)
- ✅ **Firebase Auth + Firestore is the system of record** for account, subscriptions, wallets, usage, **chats, messages, and plans**.  
- ✅ Product is designed **cloud / online first**. Web and desktop both read/write the same Firestore hub under the same login.  
- ✅ Same account history on phone web ≡ desktop (including when desktop hosts the web UI).

> **عربي:** قسم — Optional (not the base)

### Optional (not the base)
- [ ] **Local DB (VigilDB / SQLite / on-disk cache) is OPTIONAL** — for offline cache, performance, or air-gapped preference — **not** the primary source of truth.  
- [ ] If local cache exists: it **mirrors** Firestore; conflicts resolve toward cloud when online.  
- [ ] User/settings may offer “prefer offline cache” later; default product path remains **online Firestore**.

> **عربي:** قسم — Still local-only (never cloud)

### Still local-only (never cloud)
- Workspace source code, git objects, deep code index blobs, OS keychain secrets (unless a future BYOK vault is explicitly designed).

